% profile: step=one
% The guards of CHR as tcalc's: X \== Y is /=, X < Y and X =< Y order
% integers.  On the ground constraints here they mean what they mean in CHR.
% (CHR's X \== Y also holds while X is unbound; tcalc's asks every solution.)
item(1). item(2). item(3). item(b).
keep @ item(X) <=> X \== b, 1 < X, X =< 2 | kept(X).
